# Cloudflare _headers — security + caching.
# The @astrojs/cloudflare adapter appends its own immutable rule for /_astro/* at build; everything below covers the rest.
# The CSP is ENFORCED, so a new external origin fails silently until it is allowlisted here. There is no reporting endpoint, so a violation is invisible in production: to find one, read DevTools -> Issues, or the `inspector-issues` audit in a Lighthouse run.
# 'unsafe-inline' covers the inline theme/consent/demo scripts and style attributes, acceptable on a static site with no user input. Hashing them instead was considered and declined: Vite inlines bundles under assetsInlineLimit, so a bundle crossing that line changes the hash SET, not just a hash, and the CSP would have to be generated per build to keep up.
# Cloudflare Web Analytics is off (its beacon slowed LCP), which is why static.cloudflareinsights.com is absent from script-src/connect-src.
#
# img-src deliberately does NOT carry googletagmanager.com. gtag occasionally fires an image beacon to /td (twice across 150 measured page loads), the CSP blocks it, and Chrome logs a CSP issue that fails Lighthouse's `inspector-issues` audit for a 4-point best-practices drop on whichever page caught it. That is the policy working: the beacon is an ad-tech ping this site denies everywhere else. Do not allowlist it to buy the score back.
# connect-src keeps region1.google-analytics.com even though US-run measurement never touches it — that is the endpoint EEA visitors hit, i.e. exactly the ones who had to opt in.
#
# X-Frame-Options is deliberately redundant with frame-ancestors 'none', for browsers predating CSP frame-ancestors. Not dead weight; do not delete it as a duplicate.
# Permissions-Policy names every feature this site does not use. interest-cohort was removed rather than kept: FLoC was abandoned in 2022 and browsing-topics, its live successor, is already denied.
# Comments live here at column 0, never indented inside a rule block — only a leading # is documented as a comment, and an indented one risks being read as a header name.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=(), midi=(), serial=(), hid=(), bluetooth=(), idle-detection=(), local-fonts=(), browsing-topics=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://www.google-analytics.com; font-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com; connect-src 'self' https://www.google-analytics.com https://region1.google-analytics.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; upgrade-insecure-requests

# ===== A year, immutable =====
# These URLs are contract-named and unhashed (@font-face, preloads and the per-slug video conventions all hardcode them), so replacing a file's BYTES without changing its NAME will not reach a returning visitor for up to a year. To reach everyone, rename the file or drop `immutable` first. Adding a new slug or face is always safe.
#
# Replaced in place, knowingly: the Clash faces on 2026-07-15 (a cached subset still carries every glyph the site renders), and the sportime-clubs + agency-fiveeighty hero audio on 2026-07-27 (picture unchanged, so a stale copy is only missing an audio re-mix on a click-to-play video).

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Video only. Hero posters go through the image pipeline into /_astro/*, so they are content-hashed and a re-export reaches everyone.
/hero/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/wc/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/ov/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Concept microsite fonts, same contract as /fonts/*. Listed per slug because only one trailing wildcard is reliable, and a bare /concepts/* would sweep the microsite HTML into a year of caching.
/concepts/level/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/concepts/the-ninth/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/concepts/wisp/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ===== 30 days =====
# Unhashed and contract-named like the sets above, but redrawn occasionally. Long enough to kill per-navigation revalidation, short enough that replacing one in place still reaches people.
/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
/favicon-16x16.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
/favicon-32x32.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
/favicon-96x96.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
/site.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
/android-chrome-192x192.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
/android-chrome-512x512.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
/og/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
/llms.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

# ===== A day =====
# The resume is replaced during an active search and is downloaded, not just rendered. A month of caching would hand a recruiter a superseded copy.
/pratik-mehta-resume.pdf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate

# ===== Revalidate every navigation =====
# Stated rather than inherited, so the policy is this repo's choice and not the platform default. A zero lifetime with must-revalidate lets a deploy reach a returning visitor immediately while still allowing a 304.
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
# The concept microsites' analytics pair. Unhashed and contract-named like the immutable sets above, but they carry the consent posture, so a change to what loads and when has to reach returning visitors on the next navigation. Neither matched an immutable rule before this was written; stated now so it stays that way.
/concepts/analytics.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/concepts/ga-core.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
